# Guarded Resilience Only When Required

- Fallback or retry logic is allowed only when explicitly requested by product/business requirement.
- Any resilience branch must be intentional, bounded, and observable.

## Required conditions before adding fallback/retry

- State the explicit requirement in the PR/task context.
- Define clear trigger conditions.
- Define clear stop/exit conditions.
- Define max attempts/time budget (for retry).
- Define logging/metrics for each trigger.

## Implementation constraints

- No silent fallback.
- No unbounded retries.
- No nested fallback chains.
- Keep the primary path readable and dominant.

## Review checklist

- Why is resilience required here?
- Is root cause still being fixed in parallel?
- Can developers predict behavior from one pass of reading?
